# AI-DLC Workflow — ZeroFlight

When the user invokes AI-DLC, starts a new bolt/unit, or requests gated software development, read and follow:

`.aidlc-rule-details/` (resolved from project root)

Start with `common/process-overview.md` and `aidlc-docs/aidlc-state.md`.

## Project-specific context (always load)

- Vision: `aidlc-docs/inception/vision.md`
- Technical environment: `aidlc-docs/inception/technical-environment.md`
- Requirements: `aidlc-docs/inception/requirements.md`
- Units of work: `aidlc-docs/inception/units-of-work.md`

## ZeroFlight constraints

- Language: Go 1.25+
- Target: Raspberry Pi companion + Mamba F405 MK2 + INAV
- Protocol: MAVLink v2 (primary); MSP optional later
- Serial: `/dev/serial0` on UART6 (TX6/RX6)
- Safety: FC owns attitude/motor control; RPi owns mission/goto logic
- INAV MAVLink is partial — do not assume ArduPilot/PX4 APIs

## Gate rules

1. Write clarifying questions to `aidlc-docs/**/questions.md`, not inline chat only
2. Update `aidlc-docs/aidlc-state.md` after each approved gate
3. Application code lives in repo root (`cmd/`, `internal/`, `pkg/`) — never under `aidlc-docs/`
4. Human approval required before Construction code generation for new units

## Resume prompt

```
Go to aidlc-docs/aidlc-state.md, find the first unchecked item,
then go to the corresponding plan file and resume from that point.
```
